    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Rarity Varies (Requires Attunement)</em></p><p>Bound into this armor is a spell of level 8 or lower. The spell is determined when the armor is created and must belong to the Abjuration or Illusion school of magic. The armor has 6 charges and regains 1d6 expended charges daily at dawn. While wearing the armor, you can expend 1 charge to cast its spell.</p><p>The level of the spell bound into the armor determines the spell’s saving throw DC and attack bonus, as well as the armor’s rarity, as shown in the following table.</p><details><summary>Spell Level Table</summary><table><thead><tr><td>Spell Level</td><td>Rarity</td><td>Save DC</td><td>Attack Bonus</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cantrip</td><td>Uncommon</td><td>13</td><td>+5</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Uncommon</td><td>13</td><td>+5</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Rare</td><td>13</td><td>+5</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Rare</td><td>15</td><td>+7</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Very Rare</td><td>15</td><td>+7</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Very Rare</td><td>17</td><td>+9</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Legendary</td><td>17</td><td>+9</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Legendary</td><td>18</td><td>+10</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Legendary</td><td>18</td><td>+10</td></tr></tbody></table></details><p>@Embed[Compendium.dnd-dungeon-masters-guide.content.JournalEntry.dmgFoundryRefere.JournalEntryPage.Ok4iCgD25ENgoRxE cite=false caption=false classes=\"hide-in-embed\"]</p><p></p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-WeU90I1WQ1VuJo8c\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>When you add this item to your sheet, there are several one-time-only steps to set up the armor:</p><ol><li><p>Your GM must first specify the armor's rarity to determine the bound spell's level (expand the Spell Level table above).</p></li><li><p>Click on the <strong>Enspelled Armor</strong> in your inventory and use the enchantment activity to select the bound spell's level (you can also simply drag the relevant enchantment from the <strong>Enspelled Armor</strong>'s effects tab onto your item).</p></li><li><p>Drag the armor you would like to enspell onto the chat card.</p></li><li><p>Equip and attune to your newly enchanted armor.</p></li><li><p>Right click on your enspelled armor, select \"Edit\", change to the \"Activities\" tab, and open the Bound Spell activity.</p></li><li><p>Drag and drop your chosen spell onto the field at the top.</p><ul><li><p>If you're using a lower-level spell than the bound level you can adjust the \"Casting Level\" dropdown to the appropriate level and it will scale as expected.</p></li></ul></li></ol></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
